# Day 23

## Experiment Title

Understanding Docker Compose Services and Networking


## Objective

To study the working of services and networking in Docker Compose applications.


## Theory

In Docker Compose, services are used to define individual containers that work together as part of an application. Each service can run a different component such as a frontend server, backend server, or database.

Docker Compose automatically creates a bridge network for communication between containers. Containers inside the same Docker Compose project can communicate using their service names without requiring manual IP configuration.

This networking feature makes application deployment easier and improves communication between different services.


## Requirements

Docker Desktop

Docker Compose

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open Docker Desktop and verify that Docker services are running.

Create a Docker Compose configuration file with multiple services.

Start the Docker Compose application.

Check the list of created Docker networks.

Inspect the default network created by Docker Compose.

Verify that all containers are connected through the same network.


## Output

Docker Compose successfully created a default bridge network.

Containers were connected successfully through the Docker network.

Communication between services was established properly.


## Result

Successfully understood Docker Compose services and networking concepts.
